You are writing one short paragraph for an internal team-performance report
about {{ agent.name }}, a sales agent at {{ agent.tenant.name if agent.tenant else "this property" }}.

THEIR NUMBERS THIS PERIOD
- Leads handled: {{ scorecard.leads_handled }}
- Average response time: {{ scorecard.avg_response_seconds }}s across {{ scorecard.response_count }} replies
- Calls answered: {{ scorecard.calls_answered }}, missed: {{ scorecard.calls_missed }} ({{ scorecard.calls_missed_recovered }} recovered)
- Follow-ups: {{ scorecard.followups_completed }}/{{ scorecard.followups_total }} completed, {{ scorecard.followups_overdue }} overdue
- AI drafts: {{ scorecard.ai_drafts_approved }} approved / {{ scorecard.ai_drafts_rejected }} rejected of {{ scorecard.ai_drafts_total }}
- Conversions (closed-won): {{ scorecard.conversions }}

THEIR CALLS THIS PERIOD (most recent first)
{% for c in calls %}
- [{{ c.disposition }}] {{ c.summary if c.summary else "(no AI summary available)" }}
{% endfor %}
{% if not calls %}- No calls in this period.
{% endif %}

THEIR LEADS THIS PERIOD
{% for l in leads %}
- Stage: {{ l.stage }}{% if l.occasion %}, occasion: {{ l.occasion }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if not leads %}- No leads assigned in this period.
{% endif %}

INSTRUCTIONS
- Write 3-5 sentences, plain factual prose, no bullet points, no headings.
- State ONLY what the numbers and call/lead data above actually show. Never
  invent a claim about tone, professionalism, or guest sentiment that isn't
  directly supported by a call summary or disposition above -- if the data
  is too thin to say anything specific about communication style, say so
  plainly rather than filling the gap with generic praise.
- Call out one concrete strength and one concrete area to watch, if the
  data supports both. If everything looks routine, say that plainly instead
  of manufacturing a concern.
- Do not restate the raw numbers verbatim -- they're already shown
  separately in the report. Write about what they mean.
- No greeting, no sign-off, just the paragraph itself.
